-- VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000045 VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-STORM, guard runtime_verified_share_24h).
-- WHAT WAS FOUND (read 2026-10-26 from live qnfo-audit, read-only; 24 h window ending 18:30Z):
--   remediation_verifications holds 29,197 rows in 24 hours, 19,428 of them (66.5 percent) with issue_id NULL across 522 classes, the rest 9,769 attributed to an issue. The guard runtime_verified_share_24h (8.7, target >= 25) divides
--   by all of them, so the standing-detector rows lift it: 10.3 percent of the orphan rows are runtime-observable, against 2.46 percent of the attributed ones (issue 1000045, 2026-10-24). Nobody could read the share that matters
--   for issue closure (an issue closed on evidence from a runtime vantage), only the mix.
--   The producer of the orphan rows is not a stray writer (the issue asked to locate it): they are the verifications of the 549 contracts that guard no issue (issue_id NULL: failure-mode detectors fm- 15,937 rows and 409
--   classes, runtime-liveness rt- 1,845, belief- 1,022, goal- 542, slice- 82 in 24 hours), written by scripts/remediation_consumer.py and qnfo-fleet-control's remediation tick. The consumer reads each contract again 22 minutes after the
--   last read (next_due_offset, REMEDIATION-2X-1, owner directive 2026-10-13: every remediation and consumer run at least twice as fast), so a detector writes 35 to 65 rows a day. That is a chosen cadence on a chosen population, and
--   recording it hourly instead would cut 28 percent of the rows and leave the share unchanged, so the rows stay where they are (decision below) and the measurement is what changes.
-- WHAT THIS FILE DOES (migration only; the guard keeps its definition and its target, as issue 1000045 asks):
--   1. Two metrics: attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h (guard: the same formula as runtime_verified_share_24h over the attributed rows only) and orphan_verification_rows_24h (operational: the standing-detector volume). Both carry
--      their named trigger exemption in the formula text, as roadmap_items_deployed_7d does: the lever of the share is more runtime contracts on issues (RUNTIME-LIVENESS-GAP-*), which the trigger of runtime_verified_share_24h already
--      drives, and a target of 0 for the orphan volume would be unmeetable by design (the shape of issue 1000038).
--   2. fleet_tasks metric-refresh (METRIC-REFRESH-1, issue 1411) gets one step, attributed-share, that writes both every run (appended with json_insert at steps[#], the pattern of migrations/2026-10-02-act-bridge-doer-metrics.sql).
--      The same UPDATE runs here so both read a value at apply.
--   3. Issue 1000045 gets a closing probe on its own definition of done: both measures exist, are fresh within 180 minutes and agree with a live recount (orphan count within 25 percent, share within 2 points). It also gets
--      a FINDING block with the producer and the decision, and one decision_log row.
-- PREDICTION: within 120 minutes of apply attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h reads about 2.5 and orphan_verification_rows_24h about 19,000, the probe of issue 1000045 passes and closes it. runtime_verified_share_24h is
--   unchanged. The honest reading of the scoreboard becomes: 8.7 is the mix, about 2.5 is the evidence quality of issue closure, and that is what the RUNTIME-LIVENESS-GAP work lifts.
-- spof-review: none added. No DELETE or DROP runs in this file, so it names no BACKUP table beyond the two it creates for the Rollback.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- BACKUP: bak_20261026_voh1_workflow
-- Rollback: UPDATE fleet_tasks SET definition = json_remove(definition, '$.steps[' || (SELECT j.key FROM json_each(fleet_tasks.definition, '$.steps') j WHERE json_extract(j.value, '$.name') = 'attributed-share') || ']'), version = version + 1, updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 'metric-refresh' AND instr(definition, '"attributed-share"') > 0; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = (SELECT b.status FROM bak_20261026_voh1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), last_verdict = (SELECT b.last_verdict FROM bak_20261026_voh1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), verify_probe = (SELECT b.verify_probe FROM bak_20261026_voh1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), action = (SELECT b.action FROM bak_20261026_voh1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), precondition = (SELECT b.precondition FROM bak_20261026_voh1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), module = (SELECT b.module FROM bak_20261026_voh1_contract b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), attempts = 0 WHERE class = 'issue-1000045' AND module = 'verification-orphan-honest-1'; UPDATE agent_issues SET description = substr(description, 1, instr(description, char(10) || 'FINDING 2026-10-26 (rem-a2, VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1)') - 1) WHERE id = 1000045 AND instr(description, char(10) || 'FINDING 2026-10-26 (rem-a2, VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1)') > 0; DELETE FROM metric_registry WHERE metric IN ('attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h', 'orphan_verification_rows_24h'); DELETE FROM metric_authorship WHERE metric IN ('attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h', 'orphan_verification_rows_24h');

-- 0. Backups for the Rollback.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_voh1_workflow AS SELECT id, definition, version FROM fleet_tasks WHERE id = 'metric-refresh';

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_voh1_contract AS SELECT class, issue_id, status, last_verdict, verify_probe, action, precondition, module, attempts FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'issue-1000045';

-- 1. The two metrics (state UNMEASURED until the UPDATE below).
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO metric_registry (metric, layer, kind, formula, source_of_truth, baseline, target, owner, disposition_actor, refresh_cadence, warning_band, kill_band, last_value, last_refreshed, state, refresh_class) VALUES
  ('attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h', 'system', 'guard',
   '100 * remediation_verifications of the last 24h WITH an issue_id whose transport is trusted = 1, independent = 1 and runtime_observable = 1 in transport_trust / all remediation_verifications of the last 24h with an issue_id; n/a with none. The twin of runtime_verified_share_24h with the standing-detector rows (issue_id NULL) out of the denominator, so the evidence quality of issue closure is visible apart from the mix (VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1, agent_issues 1000045). Trigger exemption: runtime_verified_share_24h, which keeps its definition and its target, has the trigger that acts, and the lever is the same (more runtime contracts on issues, RUNTIME-LIVENESS-GAP-*), so a second trigger would file one breach twice',
   'qnfo-audit.remediation_verifications + transport_trust, written hourly by fleet_tasks metric-refresh (step attributed-share)',
   '2.46 on 2026-10-24 (176 of 7,160 attributed rows, agent_issues 1000045)',
   '>= 25 (the target of runtime_verified_share_24h, kept)',
   'qnfo-ops', 'the trigger of runtime_verified_share_24h: add runtime contracts on issues', 'hourly', '< 20', '< 10', NULL, NULL, 'UNMEASURED', 'computed'),
  ('orphan_verification_rows_24h', 'system', 'operational',
   'COUNT(*) of remediation_verifications of the last 24h with issue_id NULL: the verifications of the contracts that guard no issue (failure-mode, runtime-liveness, belief, goal and slice contracts), each read about every 22 minutes by REMEDIATION-2X-1. Reported next to runtime_verified_share_24h so the mix is visible (VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1, agent_issues 1000045). Trigger exemption: it is a volume chosen by the verification cadence and the number of standing detectors, not a defect to drive to 0 (a target of 0 would be unmeetable by design, the shape of agent_issues 1000038), and the share it dilutes already has a trigger',
   'qnfo-audit.remediation_verifications, written hourly by fleet_tasks metric-refresh (step attributed-share)',
   '19,428 of 29,197 rows on 2026-10-26',
   'informational (no bound)',
   'qnfo-ops', 'none: reported with runtime_verified_share_24h', 'hourly', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'UNMEASURED', 'computed');

-- 2. The refresh step, appended once (the instr guard makes a replay a no-op), and the same refresh now.
UPDATE fleet_tasks
SET definition = json_insert(definition, '$.steps[#]', json('{"type":"sql","db":"AUDIT","name":"attributed-share","sql":"UPDATE metric_registry SET last_value = CASE metric WHEN ''attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h'' THEN (SELECT CASE WHEN COUNT(*) > 0 THEN CAST(ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN t.trusted = 1 AND t.independent = 1 AND t.runtime_observable = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*), 1) AS TEXT) ELSE ''n/a'' END FROM remediation_verifications v LEFT JOIN transport_trust t ON t.transport = v.transport WHERE v.issue_id IS NOT NULL AND replace(substr(v.verified_at, 1, 19), ''T'', '' '') >= datetime(''now'', ''-1 day'')) WHEN ''orphan_verification_rows_24h'' THEN CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM remediation_verifications v WHERE v.issue_id IS NULL AND replace(substr(v.verified_at, 1, 19), ''T'', '' '') >= datetime(''now'', ''-1 day'')) AS TEXT) ELSE last_value END, last_refreshed = strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now''), state = ''MEASURED'' WHERE metric IN (''attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h'', ''orphan_verification_rows_24h'')"}')),
    version = version + 1, updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
WHERE id = 'metric-refresh' AND instr(definition, '"attributed-share"') = 0;

UPDATE metric_registry SET last_value = CASE metric WHEN 'attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h' THEN (SELECT CASE WHEN COUNT(*) > 0 THEN CAST(ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN t.trusted = 1 AND t.independent = 1 AND t.runtime_observable = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*), 1) AS TEXT) ELSE 'n/a' END FROM remediation_verifications v LEFT JOIN transport_trust t ON t.transport = v.transport WHERE v.issue_id IS NOT NULL AND replace(substr(v.verified_at, 1, 19), 'T', ' ') >= datetime('now', '-1 day')) WHEN 'orphan_verification_rows_24h' THEN CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM remediation_verifications v WHERE v.issue_id IS NULL AND replace(substr(v.verified_at, 1, 19), 'T', ' ') >= datetime('now', '-1 day')) AS TEXT) ELSE last_value END, last_refreshed = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'), state = 'MEASURED' WHERE metric IN ('attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h', 'orphan_verification_rows_24h');

-- 3. Issue 1000045: a closing probe on its definition of done (it stood on the generic superseded contract), the finding, the decision.
UPDATE remediation_contracts
SET verify_probe = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM metric_registry WHERE metric IN (''attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h'', ''orphan_verification_rows_24h'') AND state = ''MEASURED'' AND last_value IS NOT NULL AND last_refreshed >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-180 minutes'')) <> 2 THEN ''not met: the attributed share and the orphan row count are not both measured within 180 minutes'' WHEN ABS(CAST((SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''orphan_verification_rows_24h'') AS REAL) - (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM remediation_verifications WHERE issue_id IS NULL AND replace(substr(verified_at, 1, 19), ''T'', '' '') >= datetime(''now'', ''-1 day''))) > 0.25 * (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM remediation_verifications WHERE issue_id IS NULL AND replace(substr(verified_at, 1, 19), ''T'', '' '') >= datetime(''now'', ''-1 day'')) THEN ''not met: orphan_verification_rows_24h differs from the live count by more than 25 percent'' WHEN ABS(CAST((SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h'') AS REAL) - COALESCE((SELECT CASE WHEN COUNT(*) > 0 THEN ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN t.trusted = 1 AND t.independent = 1 AND t.runtime_observable = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*), 1) ELSE NULL END FROM remediation_verifications v LEFT JOIN transport_trust t ON t.transport = v.transport WHERE v.issue_id IS NOT NULL AND replace(substr(v.verified_at, 1, 19), ''T'', '' '') >= datetime(''now'', ''-1 day'')), 0)) > 2.0 THEN ''not met: attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h differs from the live value by more than 2 points'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
    verify_transport = 'd1-query', status = 'active', last_verdict = NULL, attempts = 0, deferred_since = NULL, next_due_at = datetime('now'), module = 'verification-orphan-honest-1',
    precondition = 'issue 1000045 is open: the orphan rows mask the attributed runtime share and no measure separated them',
    action = 'MEASURES the definition of done: attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h and orphan_verification_rows_24h are both measured within 180 minutes and agree with a live recount (orphan count within 25 percent, share within 2 points). VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1'
WHERE class = 'issue-1000045' AND issue_id = 1000045 AND status = 'superseded' AND instr(action, 'VACUOUS-PROBE-V3-1') = 1
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = 1000045 AND status = 'open');

UPDATE agent_issues
SET description = description || char(10) || 'FINDING 2026-10-26 (rem-a2, VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1): the producer is not a stray NULL writer. The 19,428 rows of the last 24 hours with issue_id NULL (66.5 percent of 29,197) are the verifications of 549 contracts that guard no issue (failure-mode fm- 15,937 rows over 409 classes, runtime-liveness rt- 1,845, belief- 1,022, goal- 542, slice- 82), written by scripts/remediation_consumer.py (about 22 minutes after each read, REMEDIATION-2X-1) and the qnfo-fleet-control remediation tick. The code-task line above names the wrong file: the tick binds c.issue_id and does not write them. Done by migrations/2026-10-26-verification-orphan-honest-1.sql: the guard runtime_verified_share_24h keeps its definition and target, and attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h (the attributed rows only) and orphan_verification_rows_24h are measured hourly by fleet_tasks metric-refresh. Not done, by decision: moving or attributing the orphan rows (recording them hourly would cut 28 percent of the rows and leave the share unchanged, and they are the evidence ledger of the standing detectors). The lever of the share is more runtime contracts on issues (RUNTIME-LIVENESS-GAP-*). Closing probe: contract issue-1000045.'
WHERE id = 1000045 AND status = 'open' AND instr(description, 'FINDING 2026-10-26 (rem-a2, VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1)') = 0;

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'rem-a2 (remediation session 2026-10-26)',
  'a mix is not a quality: a share whose denominator is dominated by standing-detector rows cannot say whether issue closures are confirmed from a runtime vantage, and the right answer is to measure the attributed share beside it, not to change the guard or to hide the rows',
  'VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1: metrics attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h and orphan_verification_rows_24h registered (named trigger exemptions), step attributed-share appended to fleet_tasks metric-refresh, closing probe and FINDING block on agent_issues 1000045; the orphan rows are kept in remediation_verifications by decision',
  'read 2026-10-26 from live qnfo-audit: 29,197 rows in 24 hours, 19,428 with issue_id NULL over 522 classes (fm 15,937, rt 1,845, belief 1,022, goal 542, slice 82), 9,769 attributed, runtime_verified_share_24h 8.7 against target 25, 549 contracts with issue_id NULL (529 active), next_due_offset in scripts/remediation_consumer.py gives 22 minutes for an hourly contract (REMEDIATION-2X-1), the verifier column names the consumer (remediation-consumer@sha) for about 13,000 of the orphan rows and the tick for about 1,600',
  'applied through the canonical path on merge: two metrics read a value within an hour and the probe of issue 1000045 passes',
  'two metric_registry rows (two metric_authorship probation rows by trigger), one appended workflow step, one contract and one issue description, no guard, trigger, worker, secret or verification row is touched',
  'the Rollback header of migrations/2026-10-26-verification-orphan-honest-1.sql removes the step by name, restores the contract of issue 1000045 from bak_20261026_voh1_contract, strips the FINDING block and deletes the two metric rows',
  'attributed-share-measured',
  'within 120 minutes of apply: attributed_runtime_verified_share_24h about 2.5, orphan_verification_rows_24h about 19,000, issue 1000045 closed by its own probe, runtime_verified_share_24h unchanged',
  NULL,
  'node:sqlite replay (migrations/verification-orphan-honest-1.test.mjs) with attributed and orphan rows, the stored step run on fixtures, the probe run met and unmet, apply_migrations.py --check'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE actor LIKE 'rem-a2%' AND instr(action, 'VERIFICATION-ORPHAN-HONEST-1') > 0);
